WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.370
There's no doubt that Avengers: Endgame is
going to be one of the most defining flicks

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.480
of 2019.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:10.040
From marketing efforts to storytelling promises,
from the all-star cast to the movie's title,

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.520
here are the things that Endgame has already
hit right out of the park.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.960
These days, it's almost impossible to avoid
spoilers for upcoming films.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.840
And the bigger the movie, the worse it is.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.439
From rabid fans spreading rumors to paparazzi
crashing fim sets to leaks from within the

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:27.609
studios themselves, spoilers are plastered
across the internet.

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:31.380
In fact, many movies these days spoil the
plot in their own trailers!

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.000
It can be a real bummer for fans who want
to be surprised.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.140
All of which makes the marketing campaign
for Avengers: Endgame so amazing.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.560
Not only has Marvel managed to keep any real
spoilers from slipping out, they also released

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:47.020
several gripping trailers and teasers that
somehow ratcheted up excitement without actually

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.700
telling us much of anything at all.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:53.260
Even the name of the film itself was a closely
guarded secret until the first teaser hit

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.120
in December.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.480
And even when fans guessed something correctly,
Marvel was great about… well, completely

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.660
lying in order to keep their secrets.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.900
When directly asked if the title of the fourth
Avengers film was spoken by a character in

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:09.920
Avengers: Infinity War, co-director Joe Russo
offered up a terse and direct "No," sending

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.380
fans in another direction.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:12.920
But that was a dang lie!

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:14.780
"We're in the endgame now."

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.700
Well played, Marvel.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.340
Well played.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.020
The complete lack of information has actually
helped fuel excitement among fans, as they've

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.120
been forced to make up their own theories,
which have since been debated endlessly online.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.659
And the less they tell us, the more we want
to know.

00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:33.020
It's all a testament to the tremendous cliffhanger
Marvel left us with at the end of Avengers:

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:33.800
Infinity War.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.120
Ending one of the biggest, most anticipated
films in history with the good guys losing

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:42.760
and almost everyone dead was a massive risk,
and it's one that has paid off in spades.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.200
Since the beginning of the MCU, Marvel has
put as much emphasis on fun as they do on

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:48.860
action:

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:52.600
"And three...two...one…"

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:01.750
So shifting to the kind of downbeat story
that Infinity War delivered and Endgame promises

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.260
would seem like a dramatic shift.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.640
And it is, emphasis on the drama part.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:10.330
One of the few constant criticisms of the
movies taking place in the MCU has been that

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.160
the stories' stakes aren't high enough.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.550
For instance, in Captain America: Civil War,
the massive battle between superheroes had

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:19.910
only one temporary casualty in the form of
War Machine.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.820
And by the end of the movie, he was back to
cracking jokes:

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.180
"Are you Tony Stank?"

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:26.500
"Yes.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.320
This is, this is Tony Stank.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:29.980
You're in the right place.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.440
Thank you for that."

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.500
Luckily, the Russo brothers knew that an event
like Avengers: Endgame needed something more

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.800
real, because it needed to actually matter
to fans.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.720
Anthony Russo declared that:

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:44.800
"Unless you have real stakes, you're sort
of limited in terms of the emotional impact

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.120
a story can have on you…

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.880
What we're looking for in storytelling or
art is emotional catharsis.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.700
And that's not simply getting what you want.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:56.020
It's getting an emotional experience that
makes you feel and respond to it and energizes

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:57.080
you on some level."

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.300
Co-director Joe Russo added that:

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:04.020
"This is a fantasy world, and yes, remarkable
things can happen in a fantasy world, [but]

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.780
they come at an incredibly high cost."

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:11.020
Right from the start, Marvel has been up front
about its master plan, with its Phase 1 films

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:15.090
leading into its Phase 2 films, which led
to its Phase 3 films, which led to…

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.100
Avengers: Endgame.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:21.060
So after 21 films and 11 years of buildup,
it's fitting that Endgame is poised to tie

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:24.120
together every corner of the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.700
This process already began in Infinity War,
which brought together the straightforward

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:33.040
superhero world of the Avengers with the cosmic
action of the Guardians of the Galaxy and

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.900
the mystic might of the Sorcerer Supreme,
Doctor Strange.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:40.440
And Endgame seems like it'll go even further,
with Ant-Man and the Quantum Realm set to

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.940
play a central role in the fight against Thanos.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:47.620
Until now, even with two films under his belt,
it's felt like Ant-Man has been on the fringes

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:48.620
of the MCU.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:52.760
But with the littlest Avenger potentially
playing the biggest part, Marvel has managed

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:57.540
to do the impossible: make moviegoers truly
care about nearly every character appearing

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.360
in more than 40 hours of films.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:04.000
Finally, Avengers: Endgame is already doing
something right simply by being what it's

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.640
name implies: an ending.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:09.990
One of the big problems with comic books,
or movie franchises, or TV shows, is that

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.820
the stories are pretty much all middle.

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:16.120
You get the origin, and then the adventures
go on and on and on… but nothing ever ends

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:17.360
or truly changes.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:20.340
Because then there wouldn't be a franchise
to earn more and more money.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:23.789
Avengers: Endgame, though, has set itself
up as an actual ending.

00:04:23.789 --> 00:04:26.159
Not for the entire Marvel Cinematic Universe,
of course.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.120
We all know there will be future films in
the MCU, though exactly what they'll be is

00:04:30.129 --> 00:04:34.360
another spoiler Marvel is holding on to until
after Endgame, uh, ends.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.389
But it certainly looks as though Endgame will
provide some closure to the MCU as we've known

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:39.040
it so far.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:44.000
As the trailer suggests, major characters
like Iron Man, Thor, and Captain America form

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.200
the foundation of the MCU, and one or more
of them are likely to see their stories come

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.200
to a conclusion.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.060
And it's not just them: characters like Hawkeye...

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:56.780
Gamora... and Bruce Banner all have questions
to be answered and character arcs to complete.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:59.840
Don't expect all you favorite characters to
get happy endings, though.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.220
Thanks in part to the recent acquisition of
Fox by parent company Disney, Marvel has a

00:05:04.229 --> 00:05:08.460
whole new wave of heroes they can feature
in upcoming phases, like the X-Men and the

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.460
Fantastic Four.

00:05:09.629 --> 00:05:13.760
That gives them the unusual luxury of being
able to afford to give a proper, and final,

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:17.340
farewell to some of their biggest characters
and franchises so far.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:20.800
Because they don't have to worry about the
box office, all they have to worry about is

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:24.900
making a good story that will satisfy fans
who have spent a decade of their lives getting

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.920
invested in the fate of the Avengers.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:31.200
And so far, it sure looks as though Marvel
is going to make good on just about all their

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:31.700
promises.

